<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amar Singh of Patiala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1748">1748</a>–<a href="/years/1782">1782</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amar Singh was raja of Patiala from 1765 to 1782, grandson and successor of its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-singh">Ala Singh</a>. He received the title Raja-i-Rajgan from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> and enlarged the state through campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, making Patiala the leading Phulkian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amar-singh-of-patiala.jpg" alt="Amar Singh of Patiala" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miniature_painting_of_Raja_Amar_Singh_of_Patiala,_ca.1830.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
